# Build context for the service images (services/*/Dockerfile), which are built from the
# repository root. Allow-list: everything is excluded, then only what an image needs comes back.
# Docker applies the LAST pattern that matches a path, so the exclusions after the `!` lines win.
# tests/tooling/test_container_images.py checks this file.

# 1. Nothing by default: .git, .worktrees, .venv, web/ (and web/node_modules), infra/ (Terraform
#    state, plans, .terraform, tfvars), scripts/, docs/ and the root files stay out.
*

# 2. The only inputs an image installs: the shared libraries and the services.
!libs/
!services/

# 3. Never inside libs/ or services/ either: secrets and key files, local environments, caches,
#    build output and tests (images do not run tests).
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*credentials*.json
**/*service-account*.json
**/*sa-key*.json
**/client_secret*.json
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.tfvars
**/*.tfplan
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/build
**/dist
**/tests
**/Dockerfile
